    "explanation": "To the rider (R-47539) and the driver (D-54113): the SGD 5.00 no-show fee stands and is payable to the driver as compensation.\n\nThis was an on-demand trip with no scheduled pickup time, so under POL-NS-21 the 5-minute (300 s) free wait ran from the driver's arrival. The trip record (EV-TRIP-05051) puts arrival at 08:04:20 and the wait expiry at 08:09:20; the driver cancelled at 08:10:05, i.e. 345 s after arrival, 45 s past expiry. The arrival is independently corroborated by the GPS trace (EV-GPS-05051: nearest fix 3.74 m from the pickup with 4 m reported accuracy, inside the 50 m STANDARD radius and the 25 m accuracy filter; trace COMPLETE, weight 1.0, no gap over 30 s). The driver also met the POL-NS-23 contact obligation: in-app messages at 08:04:40 and 08:08:30 (EV-CHAT-05051) and an in-app call at 08:07:10 (EV-TRIP-05051), all before cancelled_at 08:10:05. The fee-voiding limb of POL-NS-23 therefore does not fire.\n\nThe amount charged is SGD 5.00 (EV-FARE-05051: fee_charged_sgd 5.00, payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00), exactly the policy no-show fee (policy_fee_sgd 5.00), so the fee stands. POL-NS-22 makes the ruling DRIVER_COMPENSATION with both amount fields carrying the SGD 5.00 the ruling moves. No POL-NS-22 fee-mismatch referral arises (5.00 charged against a 5.00 policy fee); no POL-NS-24 goodwill credit arises (that credit needs a failure to attempt contact, which did not happen); no POL-NS-25 repeat no-show referral arises (the rider profile carries no no_show_cancellations_30d counter, and POL-NS-25 applies only when that field is present).\n\nOn your delay explanation: coming down late and a slow lift do not displace the driver's entitlement to cancel once the free wait expired. The traffic advisory you would rest the delay on (EV-ADVIS-05051-01) is MISSING, weight 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, and under POL-GEN-02(3) carries no fact.\n\nEscalation is refused. The rider argued that the trip record's driver_deadline.deadline is null (on-demand trip, no scheduled time), so POL-NS-24's arrival benchmark cannot be fixed and POL-GEN-26 requires a human review. The fact the rules actually need — when the driver arrived — is established (08:04:20, EV-TRIP-05051, GPS-corroborated by EV-GPS-05051), and on an on-demand trip no rule needs a scheduled pickup time: POL-NS-21 fixes the free wait from arrival. POL-NS-24 protects a rider who cancels because the driver did not arrive on time; the driver here did arrive and the rider never cancelled, so that limb is not engaged and POL-GEN-26 is not triggered. The dispute value is SGD 5.00, below POL-GEN-22's 10.00 SGD first band, and no fraud flag is set (fraud_flags 0 on both profiles), so under POL-NS-26 and POL-GEN-22 the AI ruling is final at any confidence. Confidence is 0.90, against a cap of 1.00 set by the weight-1.0 artifacts that carry the deciding facts (EV-TRIP-05051, EV-GPS-05051, EV-CHAT-05051, EV-FARE-05051)."
