    "explanation": "This is a no-show charge of SGD 5.00 (EV-FARE-05051: cancellation_fee 5.00, total_charged 5.00, payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.0). The charge stands and moves to the driver, so the ruling is DRIVER_COMPENSATION carrying SGD 5.00 in both money fields — the amount the ruling moves, per POL-NS-22 and POL-GEN-03.\n\nWhy the fee stands. (1) Arrival. The trip record's arrival event at 08:04:20 (EV-TRIP-05051) is corroborated by the GPS trace (EV-GPS-05051): the nearest fix sits 3.74 m from the pickup with a reported accuracy of 4 m, inside the 25 m accuracy filter and well inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius, and it falls at 08:04:31, within the 120 s arrival window. The arrival test in the category policy is therefore met. (2) Free wait. This was an on-demand trip with no scheduled time, so under POL-NS-21 the 300 s free wait runs from arrival, 08:04:20, expiring at 08:09:20. The wait timer expired at 08:09:25 and the driver cancelled at 08:10:05 — 345 s after arrival, past expiry. Under POL-NS-22 a driver who cancels after the free wait may charge the 5.00 SGD no-show fee, and the record charged exactly that figure, so no POL-NS-22 fee-amount referral arises. (3) Contact obligation. POL-NS-23 requires at least one in-app chat message and at least one in-app call before cancelled_at. EV-CHAT-05051 and EV-TRIP-05051 show the driver messaged at 08:04:40 and 08:08:30 and placed an in-app call at 08:07:10 (unanswered, 25 s), all before the 08:10:05 cancellation. POL-NS-23 is met, so no full refund. (4) POL-NS-24 gives the rider nothing: it addresses a rider's no-charge cancellation where the driver failed to arrive, but the driver did arrive and did attempt contact, and the rider never cancelled at all (cancellation was by the driver under RIDER_NO_SHOW). Neither its refund limb nor its 5.00 SGD goodwill credit is engaged.\n\nThe rider's points. Her account that the lift was slow and that she came down 'maybe 2 minutes late' is not supported by any artifact: the only third-party item on her delay, the traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-05051-01, is MISSING with weight 0.0 and carries no fact under POL-GEN-02(3). Her argument that the case must escalate under POL-GEN-26 because the driver_deadline block carries deadline null is rejected: the deadline is empty because an on-demand trip has no scheduled time (POL-NS-21 fixes the wait from arrival instead), not because evidence is missing or impaired. Every fact this ruling needs — arrival at 08:04:20, wait expiry at 08:09:20, the 08:04:40 message, the 08:07:10 call, the 08:10:05 cancellation and the 5.00 SGD charge — is carried by COMPLETE weight-1.0 artifacts, so POL-GEN-26 has no work to do and ESCALATE is not the outcome. Her chat message at 08:11:40 ('sorry coming now, where are you') confirms she was still not at the pickup well after the wait had expired; her having read the driver's first message at 08:05:14 and second at 08:08:50 does not alter the driver's entitlement to cancel once the free wait lapsed.\n\nParty profiles: the rider's and driver's prior no-show and dispute counters are context only under POL-GEN-01. No fraud flag is present on either profile, and the field POL-NS-25 names (no_show_cancellations_30d) is absent from the rider profile, so no repeat no-show referral fires. The value contested is 5.00 SGD, below POL-GEN-22's 10.00 SGD first band, and POL-NS-26 makes the AI ruling on a no-show final at the fixed 5.00 SGD fee.\n\nConfidence: every artifact carrying the deciding facts (EV-TRIP-05051, EV-GPS-05051, EV-CHAT-05051, EV-FARE-05051) carries weight_multiplier 1.0, so the cap under POL-GEN-02(2) is 1.0; the required confidence is 0.0 under POL-NS-26 and POL-GEN-22. Confidence is set at 0.95. No referral is produced: the fee matches the policy figure, no goodwill credit is due, and no repeat no-show counter is present.",
